        "original_id": "b2898295-0f7f-57be-a14f-1cf65091515a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ivan Bella, Frank De Winne, Viktor Afanasyev, Jean-Pierre Haigneré\n- Organizations: Slovak Air Force, Belgian Air Component, ESA\n- Space Missions: Soyuz TM-29, Mir\n- Places: Brezno, Czechoslovakia, Slovakia, Ledeberg, Belgium\n\nFacts:\n- Frank De Winne was born on 25 April 1961 in Ledeberg, Belgium.\n- Ivan Bella was born on 25 May 1964 in Brezno, Czechoslovakia, now Slovakia.\n- Soyuz TM-29 docked with Mir on February 22 at 05:36 GMT carrying Viktor Afanasyev of Russia, Jean-Pierre Haigneré of France, and Ivan Bella of Slovakia.\n- Ivan Bella is a Slovak Air Force officer and became the first Slovak citizen to fly in space.\n- Frank De Winne is a Belgian Air Component officer and an ESA astronaut.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
